// The sheet's own duration is Concentration(60) ("every blow you land ...
// for the duration"), but every existing weapon-damage-bonus BuffKind in
// this engine (BlindingSmite/BrandingSmite/DivineSmite/SearingSmite/
// StaggeringSmite/ThunderousSmite/WrathfulSmite -- see
// assets/common/abilities/spells/gravesong/) is a one-shot "bonus on the
// NEXT weapon hit only" buff, removed the moment it triggers
// (`buff_cat: RemoveOnAttack`, `duration: None`) -- there is no continuous
// "every hit for N seconds" weapon-buff mechanism anywhere in
// common/src/comp/buff.rs. This reuses that same one-shot family
// (BrandingSmite -- "deal additional damage, no secondary effect", the
// smaller-magnitude sibling of DivineSmite, matching this being a lower-
// circle spell) rather than inventing a new persistent BuffKind. The
// "every hit for the duration" persistence rider is dropped, not carried
// through as metadata: the compendium entry lists duration: Instant,
// matching how all 7 already-shipped gravesong smites describe their own
// one-shot mechanic (checked every one -- none of them list Concentration
// either, despite some of their own sheet rows saying the same thing).
// Listing Concentration(60) here would make the in-game spellbook tooltip
// claim a 60s buffed-hits window that doesn't exist.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.1,
    cast_duration: 0.1,
    recover_duration: 0.1,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: BrandingSmite, data: BuffData(strength: 6.0, duration: None)),
    ],
    buff_cat: Some(RemoveOnAttack),
    energy_cost: 10,
    enforced_limit: true,
)
